menu "e32p: j1939"

    config E32P_J1939_ENABLE
        bool "Enable e32p_j1939 (SAE J1939 protocol layer)"
        depends on SOC_TWAI_SUPPORTED
        select E32P_TWAI_ENABLE
        default n
        help
            SAE J1939 protocol/data layer over e32p_twai: 29-bit CAN ID <-> PGN
            codec (PDU1/PDU2), source/destination addressing, and single-frame
            (<=8 byte) send/receive. The application configures and starts TWAI;
            this layer adds the J1939 node address and message framing. Transport
            (>8 byte messages) is provided by e32p_j1939tp. Selecting this pulls
            in e32p_twai.

endmenu
